WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.920
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.320
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.880
We were on The Office together.
我们一起演过《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.140
And we're best friends.
而且我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.300
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你打造了终极的《办公室》爱好者播客。

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.800
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们将通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

7
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.980
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
幕后花絮，以及大量闺蜜的故事。

8
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.020
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是“办公室女士 6.0”。

9
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.170
Hi there, Angela.
你好啊，安吉拉。

10
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.150
Well, hi there, Jenna.
噢，你好啊，珍娜。

11
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:31.770
How are you doing?
你最近怎么样？

12
00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:32.990
You know, I'm good.
你知道的，我挺好的。

13
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.750
Is that it?
就这样吗？

14
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.230
You're just good.
你只是挺好的。

15
00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.050
Now, is this one of those times when, like, you know when someone says,
话说，这是不是那种时候，就是你知道当有人问起时，

16
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:40.830
how are you doing?
你最近怎么样？

17
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:41.170
Yeah.
对。

18
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.670
And you're like, I can't get into it.
然后你就想，我简直说来话长。

19
00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.710
And so you say, I'm good.
所以你就说，我挺好的。

20
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.010
Well, here's the thing.
好吧，情况是这样的。

21
00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.070
And I think you know this about me.
我想你也很了解我这一点。

22
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:57.270
I really have a hard time, like, just saying whatever the, like, normal response is.
我真的很难去说出那种，比如很正常的标准回答。

23
00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.150
This is kind of true.
这倒是挺真实的。

24
00:00:59.390 --> 00:00:59.730
Yeah.
对。

25
00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.790
So, like, if people say, how are you?
所以，如果别人问，你好吗？

26
00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:09.150
I might just say, well, you know, today, like, everything feels a little shitty, but I'm out there.
我可能会直接说，嗯，你知道的，今天感觉所有事情都有点糟心，但我还在坚持。

27
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.110
I'm living.
我还活着。

28
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.770
I'm putting one foot in front of the other.
我正一步一个脚印地走下去。

29
00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:16.410
And then if you say that, though, people are like, okay.
而且如果你那样说了，大家的反应就会是，好吧。

30
00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:16.630
Yeah.
对。

31
00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.210
But, lady, this is why I love you.
但是，亲爱的，这就是我爱你的原因。

32
00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.910
This is very Midwest of you.
你这太中西部风格了。

33
00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.750
I notice this every time I go home to St. Louis.
每次我回圣路易斯老家时我都深有体会。

34
00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:27.830
Like, I go to the grocery store line, and I'm checking out or something.
比如我去杂货店排队结账什么的。

35
00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.550
And the person says, how are you?
然后收银员问，你最近怎么样？

36
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.470
And I say, fine.
而我说，挺好的。

37
00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.350
I give the Los Angeles response.
我给出了洛杉矶式的回答。

38
00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:33.770
Yeah.
对。

39
00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:34.950
And I say, how about you?
然后我问，你呢？

40
00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:39.090
And then they say something, like, deeply personal.
接着他们就会说一些，比如非常私人的事情。

41
00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:39.950
Yeah.
对。

42
00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.050
They're like, well, my sister was arrested last night.
他们会说，唉，我妹妹昨晚被捕了。

43
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.790
I'm like, oh, she what?
我就想，天呐，她怎么了？

44
00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:45.530
And they're like, yep.
然后他们说，对啊。

45
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.490
I mean, she's been in trouble before, but I don't know.
我是说，她以前也惹过麻烦，不过我不知道。

46
00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:48.950
It's okay.
没事的。

47
00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.190
I think we've got a lawyer.
我想我们已经请好律师了。

48
00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.150
And I'm like, oh, my gosh.
然后我就想，我的天呐。

49
00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.930
I mean, it happens all the time.
我是说，这种事经常发生。

50
00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.530
And so I think that's how you remind me of home.
所以我觉得这就是你让我感到家的感觉的原因。

51
00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:57.670
I love it.
我喜欢。

52
00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.190
I don't mind it at all.
我一点也不介意。

53
00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.150
It is true, because my family does this.
这是真的，因为我家里人就这样。

54
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.450
Like, I'll be like, you know, how's it going?
比如，我会说，你知道的，最近怎么样？

55
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:10.170
They're like, well, the cattle guard's not getting fixed because, you know,
他们就会说，噢，牛栅栏修不好了，因为，你知道的，

56
00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:11.930
Tommy went blind again.
汤米又瞎了。

57
00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.190
He's got that plate in his head, moves around every once in a while.
他脑子里装了块金属板，每隔一段时间就会移位。

58
00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:15.810
Yeah.
对。

59
00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.770
That's a real statement my mom said to me.
这是我妈对我说过的一句实话。

60
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:18.890
Yeah, I know.
对，我知道。

61
00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:19.530
Yeah.
对。

62
00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:20.650
I like it.
我喜欢。

63
00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:21.250
All right.
好吧。

64
00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.150
Makes you more interesting, personally.
从个人角度来说，这让你更有趣了。

65
00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.650
Although I have been in your position,
虽然我也经历过你的处境，

66
00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:31.230
and I have received blank stares from people when I share in the same way.
当我以同样的方式分享时，也收到过别人茫然的目光。

67
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:31.890
Yeah.
是啊。

68
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.570
Like, it just happened at a school event.
就像，刚才在学校活动上就发生了这种事。

69
00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.990
Someone asked me how I was.
有人问我最近怎么样。

70
00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.710
And I just—honestly, I didn't get a lot of sleep last night.
而我只是——说实话，我昨晚没睡好。

71
00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.070
It's not always a complaint, either.
而且这倒也不一定总是在抱怨。

72
00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.930
Like, I say good news, too.
比如，我也会说好消息。

73
00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.150
It sounds like it's always a grape, but it's not.
听起来好像总是挺棒的，其实不然。

74
00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:44.850
I will.
我会的。

75
00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.870
Like, someone's like, how's it going?
比如，有人问，最近怎么样？

76
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:46.390
Great.
太棒了。

77
00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:50.290
I just found a pair of jeans I thought I had lost for a long time,
我刚找到了一条以为早就弄丢的牛仔裤，

78
00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.770
and they're, like, really my favorite.
而且它们，怎么说呢，真的是我的最爱。

79
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:52.830
They're, like, a lucky brand.
它们是那种幸运品牌。

80
00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:53.970
They don't make them anymore.
现在不生产了。

81
00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.330
You know, like, the low-waisted ones, everything's now.
你知道的，就像低腰的那种，现在满大街都是。

82
00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:57.510
It's, like, up at your belly button.
都快提到肚脐眼了。

83
00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.530
Who needs that crap?
谁需要那种破玩意儿？

84
00:02:58.730 --> 00:02:59.970
And I might say that.
我可能会这么说。

85
00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.710
I know, but isn't that interesting?
我知道，但这不是很有趣吗？

86
00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.850
That makes for an interesting moment in a day.
这给平淡的一天制造了一个有趣的时刻。

87
00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:08.830
If you answer a question with, like, weird specificity.
如果你用一种奇怪的具体细节来回答问题的话。

88
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.070
Or it clears the room.
或者直接冷场。

89
00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:10.730
It does.
确实会。

90
00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:12.110
Okay.
好吧。

91
00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.270
What should we do?
我们该做点什么？

92
00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.150
Oh, we should do our chit-chat suggestion.
哦，我们该做闲聊建议了。

93
00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.550
Now it felt like a lot of chit-chat.
刚才感觉已经聊了很多了。

94
00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:20.630
Let's do it.
开始吧。

95
00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.090
This one is coming in from Nat S.
这条是来自密苏里州鲍德温的

96
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.130
in Baldwin, Missouri.
Nat S. 发来的。

97
00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:25.750
That's my hometown.
那我的家乡。

98
00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.010
Literally, Baldwin, Missouri is my hometown.
真的，密苏里州鲍德温就是我的家乡。

99
00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:28.570
You're kidding.
开玩笑吧。

100
00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.130
Baldwin?
鲍德温？

101
00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.050
Yeah, it's a suburb of St. Louis.
对，那是圣路易斯的一个郊区。

102
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:31.590
Okay.
好。

103
00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:32.770
All right, let's listen.
行吧，我们来听听。

104
00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.030
Hi, ladies.
嗨，女士们。

105
00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.450
This is Nat from Missouri.
我是来自密苏里州的娜特。

106
00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.930
If you had unlimited creative freedom and an endless budget,
如果你拥有无限的创作自由和无尽的预算，

107
00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.970
tell us all about the story you'd want to produce, either together or separately.
给我们讲讲你想制作的故事，可以是一起合作，也可以是各自独立创作。

108
00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:45.410
It could be a movie or a TV show.
可以是一部电影或是一部电视剧。

109
00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.230
Chat about potential casting and plot lines.
聊聊潜在的演员阵容和剧情线。

110
00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:52.810
Or maybe even chat about what kinds of stories you wish you saw more of in today's world.
或者甚至聊聊你希望当今世界能看到更多什么类型的故事。

111
00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.510
Thanks for picking my question.
谢谢你们选了我的问题。

112
00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.050
You ladies are so groovy.
女士们，你们太时髦了。

113
00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:57.410
Love you lots and keep it up.
非常爱你们，继续加油。

114
00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.650
I mean, that's a big question.
我是说，这真是个宏大的问题。

115
00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:06.590
Nat, I'm going to say there are so many stories I would love to bring to life,
娜特，我想说有太多故事我想让它们重现生机，

116
00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:08.950
so many parts I would love to play myself.
有太多角色我想亲自去扮演。

117
00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:13.810
And I don't think it's a matter of endless creative freedom or endless budget,
我不觉得这取决于无限的创作自由或无尽的预算，

118
00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:14.910
although that would help.
虽然那确实会有帮助。

119
00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:20.250
For me, it would be I need endless bandwidth and time.
对我来说，我需要的是无尽的精力和时间。

120
00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.990
I feel like—or to clone myself.
我觉得——或者把我克隆一个。

121
00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.790
I feel like there's so many things.
我觉得有太多事情了。

122
00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:27.250
I mean, the first one coming to mind is mom detectives,
我是说，脑海中浮现的第一个就是妈妈侦探，

123
00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:34.770
which I can't do because I just don't have the time to bring that into the world.
我做不了这个，因为我实在没有时间把它带到这个世界上。

124
00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:35.990
The way we would want to do it.
以我们想要的方式去做。

125
00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:36.350
Yeah.
对。

126
00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.730
Yeah, I mean, I agree.
对，我是说，我同意。

127
00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:41.210
I mean, I do love this question because it let me daydream a little.
我是说，我很喜欢这个问题，因为它让我稍微做了一下白日梦。

128
00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:46.250
Like, Nat, for one, there's a lot of great stories that haven't been told
比如，娜特，首先有很多精彩的故事还没被讲出来，

129
00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:51.030
about women who were cowgirls, like real working cowgirls.
关于身为女牛仔的女性，真正的职业女牛仔。

130
00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.350
And there's some great stories.
有一些很棒的故事。

131
00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.750
And I've read a few, and I'm like, gosh, that would make an amazing movie.
我看过几部，当时就想，天哪，拍成电影一定超棒。

132
00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:03.010
Just highlight one of them that rode horseback and worked the land just like hardcore, you know?
单单是突显其中一个策马奔腾、像硬汉一样在土地上劳作的女性，你知道吗？

133
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.170
I would love that movie.
我会很想看那部电影。

134
00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.690
Like, that would be something I would want to see.
那种题材就是我想看的。

135
00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:07.170
Yeah.
对。

136
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:11.910
So that's a story I always thought would be cool to tell, like, the women of the West, you know?
所以这是我一直觉得拍出来会很酷的故事，比如，西部女性，你知道吗？

137
00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:12.490
Yes.
对的。

138
00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.790
And then for me, also mom detectives.
然后对我来说，还有妈妈侦探。

139
00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:15.710
And I'll tell you why.
我来告诉你为什么。

140
00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.070
Jenna and I, like, we don't do anything half-ass.
詹娜和我，我们做事从不半途而废。

141
00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.130
If we were to do this, we would do it.
我们要么不做，要做就得做到位。

142
00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.830
And we don't have time to do it.
而我们现在没时间去做。

143
00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:27.390
But I even fantasize about the cast because that's where I have the most fun when I think
但我甚至连演员阵容都幻想好了，因为每当我构思项目时，最开心的就是，

144
00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.390
about projects is, like, seeing who I would want.
去想想我会选谁。

145
00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:34.390
So, Nat and Jenna, this is my daydream cast for mom detectives.
所以，娜特和詹娜，这是我心目中妈妈侦探的梦幻阵容。

146
00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:35.750
Oh, I can't wait to hear it.
哦，我等不及想听了。

147
00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:36.130
Okay.
好。

148
00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:40.550
Husbands, Steve Little, and Tone Bell.
丈夫们，史蒂夫·利特尔和托恩·贝尔。

149
00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.450
Amazing.
太棒了。

150
00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:41.990
Amazing.
太棒了。

151
00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.510
Neighbors that we drive crazy with our mom detectiveness.
被我们母亲般的侦探本能折腾得抓狂的邻居。

152
00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:47.770
Bobby Lee.
鲍比·李。

153
00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:48.390
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

154
00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:49.570
Rachel Dratch.
瑞秋·德拉彻。

155
00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.270
Timberley Hill, who is hilarious.
蒂姆伯莉·希尔，她太搞笑了。

156
00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:57.250
Then I also want the two guys across the street that hosts the Fourth of July barbecue
然后我还想要街对面每年举办独立日烧烤的那两个小伙子

157
00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:57.810
every year.
每年。

158
00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.430
This is also in my neighborhood.
这也是在我的社区里。

159
00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:03.210
They're very serious about their meat.
他们对自己的肉非常认真。

160
00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:04.470
You're going to have to go over there.
你得过去一趟。

161
00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.390
It's like a big deal.
这就像是一件大事。

162
00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:05.790
Okay.
好的。

163
00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:06.710
They're very intense.
他们非常较真。

164
00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:11.050
I want local cops that we butt heads with because we're mom detectives.
我想要当地的警察，我们因为是母亲侦探而跟他们针锋相对。

165
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.950
I want them to be Jim Gaffigan and Jason Antoon.
我希望他们是吉姆·加菲根和杰森·安图恩。

166
00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:14.610
Okay.
